<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43912" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐήμερ-ος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐάμ-</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> [ᾱ</span>], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a fine</i> or <i>prosperous day</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. φάος</span> a <i>happy</i> day, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				708
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bright, happy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐάμεροι μολπαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					773.47
				</span></i>
			 (lyr., nisi leg. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αμερίαι</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; χρόνῳ δ᾽ ἐξέλαμψεν
				εὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
				41(64).62
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσωπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1322
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοῖρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					71d
				</span></i>
			 (perh. with play on <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥμερος</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; τὸ εὐ</span>.
				<i>a prosperous life</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.515
			</span></i>.</div>
